From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Il tuo nome <tu@esempio.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 22:48:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] sb/intel/lynxpoint: Full reset to clear the FDSW lock for the
 GbE switch

pch_apply_gbe_option() writes the LAN disable bit of BUC (RCBA 0x3414
bit 5) and resets for it to take effect, but the bit lives in the SUS
well, which the Function Disable lockdown freezes (FDSW, RCBA 0x3420 bit
7). A reset after the option is toggled runs with the lockdown still set
from the boot before (it survives a warm reset), so the write does not
stick, and the code warned and gave up: on a ThinkPad W541 the Ethernet
stayed on until the next full power cycle, which clears the lockdown.

When the write does not take and FDSW is locked, do the full reset (CF9
0x0E, a platform power cycle) to clear the lockdown instead of warning:
the next boot's romstage runs before the lockdown is set again, the
write sticks there, and the following reset applies it, as the Lenovo
firmware of the W541 does (GNET94WW, PchInitPeim). The POST code of the
reset is left as before (0xfc, "GbE"), so neither reset is logged as a
hang, and the native RAM init keeps its cache across both (a fast boot).

TEST=On a ThinkPad W541 with the native RAM init: Ethernet toggled off
in the setup, BUC 0x00000000 at the boot after the save (FDSW locked),
then off and the controller gone after the firmware's own resets,
without a manual power cycle.

Change-Id: I7873b6055f048dfa72709bcf7d204b7a0b4d1ca9
---
 src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/early_pch.c | 22 +++++++++++++++++----
 src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/pch.h       |  2 ++
 2 files changed, 20 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/early_pch.c b/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/early_pch.c
index 3610c3fc5f..1a3a045bc0 100644
--- a/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/early_pch.c
+++ b/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/early_pch.c
@@ -120,12 +120,26 @@ void pch_apply_gbe_option(void)
 		return;
 
 	RCBA32(BUC) = want;
-	/* Be sure not to reset for naught: the bit may be locked */
+	/*
+	 * The LAN disable bit of BUC lives in the SUS well, which the Function
+	 * Disable lockdown (FDSW bit 7) freezes: a reset after the option is
+	 * toggled still runs with the lockdown set, so the write does not stick.
+	 * Clear the lockdown with a full reset (CF9 0x0E power cycle, which the
+	 * next boot's romstage then precedes before the lockdown is set again),
+	 * as the Lenovo firmware of the W541 does; the write takes on that boot.
+	 */
 	if (RCBA32(BUC) != want) {
-		printk(BIOS_WARNING, "GbE: BUC 0x%08x does not take the change\n", RCBA32(BUC));
-		return;
+		if (RCBA32(FDSW) & FDSW_LOCK) {
+			printk(BIOS_INFO, "GbE: BUC locked by FDSW, full reset to clear it\n");
+		} else {
+			printk(BIOS_WARNING, "GbE: BUC 0x%08x does not take the change\n",
+			       RCBA32(BUC));
+			return;
+		}
+	} else {
+		printk(BIOS_INFO, "GbE: turned %s, full reset for it to take effect\n",
+		       on ? "on" : "off");
 	}
-	printk(BIOS_INFO, "GbE: turned %s, full reset for it to take effect\n", on ? "on" : "off");
 	if (CONFIG(CMOS_POST)) {
 		cmos_post_extra(0x47624500);	/* "GbE" */
 		cmos_post_code(POSTCODE_RESET_REQUESTED);
diff --git a/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/pch.h b/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/pch.h
index 0014a68e96..22d22883c8 100644
--- a/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/pch.h
+++ b/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/pch.h
@@ -518,6 +518,8 @@ void mainboard_config_rcba(void);
 #define HPTC		0x3404	/* 32bit */
 #define GCS		0x3410	/* 32bit */
 #define BUC		0x3414	/* 32bit */
+#define FDSW		0x3420	/* Function Disable SUS Well lockdown */
+#define  FDSW_LOCK		(1 << 7)
 #define PCH_DISABLE_GBE		(1 << 5)
 #define FD		0x3418	/* 32bit */
 #define DISPBDF		0x3424  /* 16bit */
-- 
2.43.0

